{
  "title": "📊 Mode of Grouped Data — The Most Popular Value",
  "hook": "What shoe size sells the most? Which score range has the most students? The mode is the value that appears most frequently — the 'most popular' value in the dataset!",
  "explanation": "<div style=\"background:#F3E5F5;border-left:4px solid #7B1FA2;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0\"><strong style=\"color:#7B1FA2\">Modal Class:</strong> The class interval with the <b>highest frequency</b>.</div><div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E3F2FD,#BBDEFB);border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1.05rem;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-size:0.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:#1565C0;margin-bottom:4px\">Mode Formula</div><strong>Mode = l + [(f₁ − f₀) / (2f₁ − f₀ − f₂)] × h</strong></div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Symbol</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Meaning</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">l</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Lower boundary of the modal class</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">f₁</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Frequency of the modal class</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">f₀</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Frequency of the class <b>before</b> the modal class</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">f₂</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Frequency of the class <b>after</b> the modal class</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">h</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Class width</td></tr></table><div style=\"background:#F5F5F5;border-left:3px solid #4A90D9;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 12px;margin:6px 0;font-size:0.9rem\">The mode is the value in the modal class that accounts for its 'peak' — it's pulled toward the side with the bigger neighboring frequency.</div><div style=\"background:#E3F2FD;border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">ℹ️ <strong>Tip:</strong> <b>Empirical relationship:</b> 3 × Median = Mode + 2 × Mean (approximately true for moderately skewed data).</div>",
  "worked_example": "<b>Example:</b> Find the mode: 0-10 (f=5), 10-20 (f=8), 20-30 (f=15), 30-40 (f=12), 40-50 (f=10).<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Modal class: 20-30 (highest f = 15)</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>l = 20, f₁ = 15, f₀ = 8, f₂ = 12, h = 10</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Mode = 20 + (15−8)/(2×15−8−12) × 10</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div><div><strong>= 20 + 7/10 × 10 = 20 + 7 = 27</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div></div>",
  "try_this": {
    "question": "Find the mode: 10-20 (f=4), 20-30 (f=7), 30-40 (f=12), 40-50 (f=8), 50-60 (f=3).",
    "hint": "Modal class: 30-40 (f=12). f₀=7, f₂=8.",
    "answer": "Mode = 30 + (12−7)/(24−7−8) × 10 = 30 + 50/9 = 30 + 5.56 = 35.56."
  },
  "fun_fact": "In fashion, the 'mode' literally means the most popular style. The statistical term has the same origin — it identifies what's most common!"
